{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:e3c21788eb512a42daf5308c52e6685c76cdc1a8ccf2f4d5ab1ed640acf95fb8","title":"Can a low-energy Abelian gauge symmetry protect the proton without obstructing fermion masses or a neutrino seesaw? The proposed symmetry must also be family universal and anomaly free.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3a88a9420b346a55a9e9b0d0a60f6153b440a18212ffa5b088ebd4474fa0a3a","title":"Can species holography determine crossover scales, Planck hierarchies and Vainshtein scales in Cascading DGP, including a gravitational interpretation that survives gravity decoupling?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0013"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3b641ad6c4b199ac596b76670ac6ccc346ea8362654013d10c4325cec9dea7e","title":"How can approximate bulk locality, especially radial locality and reconstruction on overlapping boundary regions, emerge when the full CFT operator algebra cannot obey the apparent bulk commutation relations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3db1a2414940cae1a3d9e2dc52ae2c81b731c5780a74b6c6ae7931caafc8719","title":"Can logarithmic-Kähler α-attractor supergravity models retain their successful inflationary predictions while also describing a tiny positive vacuum energy and supersymmetry breaking of adjustable strength, without introducing an additional Polonyi scalar?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3e82001928b4336d507d35c23d8ce871275357b13cd756a353b8ce401130fa1","title":"Can quantum superpositions of spin-network geometries with different vertex spacings prevent the fermion doubling associated with discretized matter equations, thereby opening a route to chiral fermions in loop quantum gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0019"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3df5983baca584861ef45f19876dcba6c963285f1be52762f1ab5c34a2846eb","title":"Can dark ensembles with Regge spectra and exponentially growing Hagedorn degeneracies realize the abundance–lifetime balancing required by Dynamical Dark Matter, and what initial cosmological restrictions follow from their aggregate abundance and effective equation of state?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0023"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3ab8ebca9e427e55af776101a4ee2c4564b62f3eec6343a8b25bcddffa71dfa","title":"Do all string/M-theory AdS flux vacua admit a physical near-horizon brane description, and can open/closed-string interactions turn the sharpened-WGC decay argument into a perturbative instability of nonsupersymmetric AdS?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0023"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3bcd13d37f01ad803630580719e5adf81c18082990e350edd0e07f32762f563","title":"Can numerous, very soft nonthermal dark photons enhance the CMB Rayleigh–Jeans photon count without violating the constraints considered, and thereby produce a detectable 21 cm signature or explain the then-tentative unusually strong EDGES absorption?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e379119237b543c9f7ece726038a4019b30c047d7ccd48daf12e5f43986e8239","title":"Can classical massive type IIA de Sitter solutions have both large internal volume and weak string coupling, suppressing α′ and string-loop corrections? The paper also asks whether this suppression can become arbitrarily good along a family of solutions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e33478e55b0ab253ccdc50874e98772364abb288b51add1fe9ff41944f6ae1e0","title":"Can localized transplanckian scalar excursions evade gravitational censorship through smooth higher-dimensional completion, and do classical instabilities supply an alternative censorship mechanism?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e384a05394cc517f27cc51d49f1c5e2804a14aedf114bb85b95df37eb210feaa","title":"Do instanton corrections preserve a classically infinite field-space distance, or can the endpoint move to finite distance while string scales and effective-theory control deteriorate?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3bb0e31148827c89bf6e18d4a26669a33555d2e986ffbb3436d80b790179c61","title":"Can a local Argyres–Douglas singularity occur in a compact gravitational construction? The paper provides explicit Weierstrass sections whose double root permits a local analytical test of the conformal scaling geometry.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e32c7f128410233ca55ab75e01e5468626ebf2ea175a44320754dc21201ffed1","title":"The setting describes inflation driven by several scalar coordinates whose kinetic terms define a curved field space. Background trajectories and distances depend on this metric, while perturbations probe both its curvature and the potential.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3087c20523023db4cc4e7f00f8b17299031ce7e7fceba1d4ead7ccb39e51178","title":"Can negative bare vacuum energy coexist with late-time accelerated expansion when contortion contributes to gravity? The paper asks whether an apparent quintessence potential can emerge from Lorentz violation instead of requiring an elementary canonical scalar.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0043"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3ad7dce03ec05761bd2c2d58f25dc6202f573bcd1faadfff6985d5f9bf6b534","title":"What positivity inequalities on polynomials of zeta values and multiple zeta values follow from unitarity and analyticity of four-particle open- and closed-superstring tree amplitudes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3bab4a9180ade0203f4e0a68a6acdf8868aaa8e6eea84e3b8dd9810bee72e17","title":"How sensitive is charged-black-hole evaporation to the electron charge-to-mass ratio, despite the electron's large margin above the stated WGC bound, and what might this imply for extremality, the third law and cosmic censorship?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e31c329d1842884f316b2a891cce49995a64190b9b141814d0a7c413a5cdc162","title":"Can quantum-gravity higher-curvature terms relax geodesic focusing and singularity-theorem conditions? The paper distinguishes nonperturbative quadratic gravity from general relativity treated perturbatively as an effective field theory.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e344beee1ca6d2b80056745e8d8bc87ad9bd33f5aa3eee3a86fc8d74450e8d98","title":"How far can TCC bounds on inflationary energy and primordial tensors be relaxed by allowing substantial potential-energy evolution after observable modes exit, while preserving the initial nearly scale-invariant scalar spectrum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0049"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e33d632f4ff1ccd022e7ad0a70383793597d9bbd76748c7a98b8ec1b13551838","title":"Can soft directions near a low-energy minimum support slowly evolving dark energy? The paper proposes small curvatures and a hierarchy among a few fields as a possible mechanism, leaving cosmological evolution for future work.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e34ce0f747e56575ca4c58d387d250c24efbfca01930c5a7c3da82010be5fbd4","title":"How can a field-space variational formulation explain gravitational stabilization and quenching of Minkowski or AdS false-vacuum decay, characterize critical domain walls, and approximate near-critical decays beyond the thin-wall limit?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e31acda379069ee2288c4b1e39ec48b61f75cb193a07505bd397598016f500e9","title":"Could CMB spectral distortions reveal low-frequency gravitational waves produced by late-time axion–gauge quintessence?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3a9dfbfc44a651628c123662014ccb5e032d01220e4ee1b79ecb3438f5cf274","title":"Can difference equations derived intrinsically from perturbative topological-string expansions select analytic nonperturbative completions, reveal strong-coupling structure and capture universal behavior near finite-distance singularities without requiring a dual description?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3581a187356f856d52a152891645bfc03faf2c890a0a83a2ff910d8bbe867b0","title":"The retained universe has one isotropic scale factor and a homogeneous dilaton, with no Kalb-Ramond background. This setting tests whether curvature corrections alone can sustain de Sitter expansion while preserving the homogeneous string cosmology assumptions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3b88af4e4e863af2d3399a4dad82e2ee43fae4307f0c7f37df20705928cff09","title":"Under what conditions can observationally viable inflation satisfy the Trans-Planckian Censorship Conjecture (TCC), and how do its constraints on gravitational waves and initial conditions change between canonical slow-roll, modified-gravity slow-roll, and constant-roll models?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3e4ab340a75f3c98d2936f0ad8ff707de9caf898e170c72c631b12e7348e437","title":"Does the massless vacuum-distance behavior found for a scalar persist for free Dirac fermions in arbitrary spatial dimension?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e31617c9b66aa35233790aaab09e54817638253b65cefa610fd5590fa48334dd","title":"Can metric Higgs inflation, Higgs–Dilaton inflation, or Palatini Higgs inflation satisfy the further-refining de Sitter swampland conjecture together with both SWGC and its strong version?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0073"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e3df8dac4dafbfd190aed32a9f587ae75dc00e117e8d7d558a4473554acbefbe","title":"Which supergravities, matter couplings and gaugings have been constructed across dimensions, and how can their component formulations and duality-covariant descriptions be summarized?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0085"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e30ab6117d8c33fa671a4def995a59f15dc1eb97df95e432a51383fbc6d38013","title":"How does the bubble of nothing (BoN), a dynamical cobordism ending spacetime by circle pinch-off, transform under T-duality? Does the growing dual circle describe spontaneous decompactification, or does the full string configuration still terminate spacetime?","connectionC